00:35:37,567 --> 00:35:40,248
Ray-thinned are what you're thinking of when I say fish.

380
00:35:40,749 --> 00:35:42,730
Goldfish, trout, salmon, et cetera, et cetera.

381
00:35:42,910 --> 00:35:50,453
It's all those ones that have the most usually transparent, very thin fins with rays.

382
00:35:50,513 --> 00:35:56,376
Those little spines that are going through like an Asian fold-out fan.

383
00:35:56,636 --> 00:35:56,897
Yes.

384
00:35:57,164 --> 00:35:58,484
To give them support.

385
00:35:58,965 --> 00:36:02,586
Lobe-thinned fish still have those ray-fins.

386
00:36:03,086 --> 00:36:10,369
But instead of supporting them just by rays, they support them with a fleshy piece of limb.

387
00:36:10,389 --> 00:36:11,210
A lobe.

388
00:36:11,330 --> 00:36:17,812
A lobe in the fin with bones inside it, with a skeletal support system.

389
00:36:17,912 --> 00:36:22,054
So they have a small little limb that is edged by a fin.

390
00:36:22,405 --> 00:36:26,647
And that's what they use to maneuver and move around in the water.

